{"id":"7ca316f0d7623463","group":"27","path":"27/27-ex-pbextensioncontrast.md","title":"Polynomial, Lovász, and envelope values can differ","display":"ex-pbextensioncontrast — Polynomial, Lovász, and envelope values can differ","type":"example","metadata":{"type":"example","book":"Boolean Functions: Theory, Algorithms, and Applications","book_abbrev":"27","label":"27-ex-pbextensioncontrast","aliases":["27-ex-pbextensioncontrast"],"display":"ex-pbextensioncontrast — Polynomial, Lovász, and envelope values can differ","depends_on":["[[27-df-lovaszextension]]","[[27-df-pbenvelopes]]"],"source_file":"C:\\Users\\lzy\\Documents\\BaiduSyncdisk\\calibre\\Yves Crama, Peter L. Hammer\\Boolean Functions_ Theory, Algorith (5073)\\Boolean Functions_ Theory, Algo - Yves Crama, Peter L. Hammer.pdf","source_section":"§13.3.1–§13.3.3","source_statement":"Local two-variable example of the extension definitions","source_printed_pages":"579–584","source_pdf_pages":"603–608","verification_status":"proved-in-note"},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"example"},{"key":"book","html":"Boolean Functions: Theory, Algorithms, and Applications"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"27"},{"key":"label","html":"27-ex-pbextensioncontrast"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>27-ex-pbextensioncontrast</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"ex-pbextensioncontrast — Polynomial, Lovász, and envelope values can differ"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"efe2d4b0294be128\" href=\"?note=efe2d4b0294be128\" title=\"27-df-lovaszextension\">27-df-lovaszextension</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"2ad3e401f85da77f\" href=\"?note=2ad3e401f85da77f\" title=\"27-df-pbenvelopes\">27-df-pbenvelopes</a></span></div>"},{"key":"source_file","html":"C:\\Users\\lzy\\Documents\\BaiduSyncdisk\\calibre\\Yves Crama, Peter L. Hammer\\Boolean Functions_ Theory, Algorith (5073)\\Boolean Functions_ Theory, Algo - Yves Crama, Peter L. Hammer.pdf"},{"key":"source_section","html":"§13.3.1–§13.3.3"},{"key":"source_statement","html":"Local two-variable example of the extension definitions"},{"key":"source_printed_pages","html":"579–584"},{"key":"source_pdf_pages","html":"603–608"},{"key":"verification_status","html":"proved-in-note"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<p>取 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"n=2\">\\(n=2\\)</span>；<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{PolExt},\\mathrm{LovExt}\">\\(\\mathrm{PolExt},\\mathrm{LovExt}\\)</span>（see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"efe2d4b0294be128\" href=\"?note=efe2d4b0294be128\" title=\"27-df-lovaszextension\">27-df-lovaszextension</a>），<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{LowEnv},\\mathrm{UpEnv}\">\\(\\mathrm{LowEnv},\\mathrm{UpEnv}\\)</span>（see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"2ad3e401f85da77f\" href=\"?note=2ad3e401f85da77f\" title=\"27-df-pbenvelopes\">27-df-pbenvelopes</a>）。</p>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"f:\\mathbb B^2\\to\\mathbb R,\\qquad f(a)\\coloneqq a_1a_2.\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[f:\\mathbb B^2\\to\\mathbb R,\\qquad f(a)\\coloneqq a_1a_2.\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\forall p\\in U_2\\quad \\mathrm{PolExt}(f)(p)=p_1p_2,\\quad\\mathrm{LovExt}(f)(p)=\\min\\{p_1,p_2\\},\\quad\\mathrm{LowEnv}(f)(p)=\\max\\{0,p_1+p_2-1\\},\\quad\\mathrm{UpEnv}(f)(p)=\\min\\{p_1,p_2\\}.\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\forall p\\in U_2\\quad \\mathrm{PolExt}(f)(p)=p_1p_2,\\quad\\mathrm{LovExt}(f)(p)=\\min\\{p_1,p_2\\},\\quad\\mathrm{LowEnv}(f)(p)=\\max\\{0,p_1+p_2-1\\},\\quad\\mathrm{UpEnv}(f)(p)=\\min\\{p_1,p_2\\}.\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{LowEnv}(f)(\\tfrac12,\\tfrac12)=0&lt;\\mathrm{PolExt}(f)(\\tfrac12,\\tfrac12)=\\tfrac14&lt;\\mathrm{LovExt}(f)(\\tfrac12,\\tfrac12)=\\mathrm{UpEnv}(f)(\\tfrac12,\\tfrac12)=\\tfrac12.\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{LowEnv}(f)(\\tfrac12,\\tfrac12)=0&lt;\\mathrm{PolExt}(f)(\\tfrac12,\\tfrac12)=\\tfrac14&lt;\\mathrm{LovExt}(f)(\\tfrac12,\\tfrac12)=\\mathrm{UpEnv}(f)(\\tfrac12,\\tfrac12)=\\tfrac12.\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<p>本地例子，不标作原书 Example 13.5。重心分布用 t=λ(1,1) 表示，其余质量分别为 p₁−t、p₂−t、1−p₁−p₂+t；非负性恰要求 max(0,p₁+p₂−1)≤t≤min(p₁,p₂)。目标期望就是 t，故两包络如式。独立分布对应 t=p₁p₂；Lovász对应较大端点。一般定义的全实数范围由此明确区分，而非仅比较一个数值样本。</p>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"27-df-lovaszextension","status":"resolved","id":"efe2d4b0294be128","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[27-df-lovaszextension]]","embed":false},{"target":"27-df-pbenvelopes","status":"resolved","id":"2ad3e401f85da77f","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[27-df-pbenvelopes]]","embed":false},{"target":"27-df-lovaszextension","status":"resolved","id":"efe2d4b0294be128","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"取 $n=2$；$\\mathrm{PolExt},\\mathrm{LovExt}$（see [[27-df-lovaszextension]]），$\\mathrm{LowEnv},\\mathrm{UpEnv}$（see [[27-df-pbenvelopes]]）。","embed":false},{"target":"27-df-pbenvelopes","status":"resolved","id":"2ad3e401f85da77f","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"取 $n=2$；$\\mathrm{PolExt},\\mathrm{LovExt}$（see [[27-df-lovaszextension]]），$\\mathrm{LowEnv},\\mathrm{UpEnv}$（see [[27-df-pbenvelopes]]）。","embed":false}],"attachments":[],"math":[{"tex":"n=2","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{PolExt},\\mathrm{LovExt}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{LowEnv},\\mathrm{UpEnv}","display":false},{"tex":"f:\\mathbb B^2\\to\\mathbb R,\\qquad f(a)\\coloneqq a_1a_2.","display":true},{"tex":"\\forall p\\in U_2\\quad \\mathrm{PolExt}(f)(p)=p_1p_2,\\quad\\mathrm{LovExt}(f)(p)=\\min\\{p_1,p_2\\},\\quad\\mathrm{LowEnv}(f)(p)=\\max\\{0,p_1+p_2-1\\},\\quad\\mathrm{UpEnv}(f)(p)=\\min\\{p_1,p_2\\}.","display":true},{"tex":"\\mathrm{LowEnv}(f)(\\tfrac12,\\tfrac12)=0<\\mathrm{PolExt}(f)(\\tfrac12,\\tfrac12)=\\tfrac14<\\mathrm{LovExt}(f)(\\tfrac12,\\tfrac12)=\\mathrm{UpEnv}(f)(\\tfrac12,\\tfrac12)=\\tfrac12.","display":true}],"bytes":1895,"backlinks":[{"id":"5244dbb38da17b8a","anchor":"ref-596","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[27-ex-pbextensioncontrast|ex-pbextensioncontrast — Polynomial, Lovász, and envelope values can differ]]"}],"outgoing":["efe2d4b0294be128","2ad3e401f85da77f"]}